cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  caustica: GPU-accelerated nonlinear acoustic simulation for
  focused ultrasound
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Eren
    family-names: Bulbul
    email: ebulbul@yildiz.edu.tr
    affiliation: Yildiz Technical University
repository-code: https://github.com/ebx0/caustica
url: https://ebx0.github.io/caustica/
abstract: >-
  caustica simulates nonlinear acoustic propagation for focused and therapeutic
  ultrasound. A k-space pseudospectral time-domain engine solves the Westervelt
  or linear continuous-wave problem on numpy or CuPy from a single set of
  operators, a k-Wave adapter provides an independent cross-check, and a Pennes
  bioheat solver turns the acoustic field into temperature and CEM43 thermal
  dose. Runs are planned against the device before they start, stamped with the
  environment and commit that produced them, and validated against analytic
  references rather than against stored fixtures.
keywords:
  - HIFU
  - focused ultrasound
  - nonlinear acoustics
  - acoustic simulation
  - Westervelt equation
  - k-space pseudospectral method
  - thermal dose
  - GPU computing
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0.dev0
